From: suraman21 <240521193+suraman21@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:17:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Archive the prototype and lay down the app structure

The repository previously held the earlier prototype flat at the root.
That layout is what we are not adopting: its backend/ implements a
parallel API and a second staff/session model, and its database/
migrations collide with the platform's sql/001-098.

Move all six prototype folders together under
docs/prototypes/member-app-2026-11-26/ using git mv, so every file keeps
its history, and put the agreed structure at the now-empty root:

  src/{Auth,Http,Repository,Service,Support,View}
  templates/{layouts,pages}
  assets/{css,js,favicon}
  docs/  -- the handbook

The prototype is reference material only. Only frontend/ is intended for
reuse, and even then js/session.js must be replaced rather than adapted.

Add docs/00-START-HERE.md for a cold start: what this repository is, how
to get it running, the six facts that change design decisions, and what
to read in what order. HANDBOOK links to it from the top.

Documentation adjustments for the move:
- members/ no longer exists, so paths and link targets are root-relative
- 06 section 1 is marked done, recording what the move actually involved
  (including the prototype's own docs/ collision)
- HANDBOOK correction 3 now states the separation as fact

No behaviour is included.
